==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|bodies|lang=en}}, plural of {{term|body||lang=en|upper part of a dress}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɒdɪs/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈbɑːdɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|bodices}}

# An [[article]] of [[clothing]] for women, covering the body from the neck to the waist, lacking sleeves or with detachable sleeves.
# A woman's blouse-like garment, especially with European folk dress.
#*{{quote-book|year=1956|author=[[w:Delano Ames|Delano Ames]]|title=Crime out of Mind|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5915292W|passage=On the cover of the leaflet advertising the Alpenrose Gasthof in Zirl am Gurgl […] there is a decorative picture of a young woman.  She is wearing Tyrolese costume: the low-cut white '''bodice''' with cross-laced velvet waistcoat, the floral apron and dirndl skirt.}}
# The upper portion of a one- or two-piece dress, in distinction to the skirt and sleeves.
# {{context|archaic|lang=en}} A kind of under waist stiffened with whalebone, etc., worn especially by women; a corset; stays.

====Derived terms====
